CARRY-FORWARD OBLIGATION
====================================================================================
This block PRESCRIBES:
  (i)   TWO rows on the data-port readback after a non-packet command, values 5a and a5;
  (ii)  a MEASURED score out of 26 for every mutant cited in THIS round's record.
        *** SCOPED, after the fable5 seat caught the first wording licensing a records
        crime. ***  It read "the old `x/22` figures become wrong records the moment the
        rows land."  They do not: #495's `x/22` numbers are TRUE measurements of the
        11-row instrument and stay true forever.  What would be wrong is citing them as
        scores of the CURRENT detector.  As first written this clause authorised editing
        another round's correct records, which is the opposite of what it is for;
  (iii) an explicit no-row sentence for the self-normalising claim (block 2), which is
        true and unobservable on the shipped build;
  (iv)  a sentence in the probe naming the `overread -1` cross-dependency (block 1);
  (v)   an IN-PLACE correction of the `wdcatapistswap` ledger row, whose filed note
        carries the same wrong post-packet sentence the amendment refutes -- a wrong
        record survives being superseded, so it is corrected where it sits;
  (vi)  the flag-implies-phase invariant carried into the probe as the M rows'
        non-vacuity warrant, since it is what makes them undodgeable by a phase edit.

If the row list is later rewritten from the pass-2 panel's findings, it must be DIFFED
against these four, not merely extended -- #490 lost both of its prescribed rows exactly
that way, three hours after prescribing them.
